      "mergeID": "5ad988adc1931344cfc4b821",
      "mergedPostDetails": "This is something I've thought about for a while. But I think it would be cool for users to be able to set a world as their default world to load into when they start the app without having to mess with startup commands. Maybe that could open the possibilities for user build hub like areas, or just to just load into a private instance of Avatar Testing on startup.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "In-game option to change world you load into on startup",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "58cb5986ea9d1d76eccae48b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "This is something I personally think would be very cool.  However one of the problems it could introduce with a relatively small community is you end up with a situation where there is nobody in the actual default load in world where people come into.  Once we are in the thousands of users, I could see something like this working though.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
